Z||000000||sid1200||07-29-99||01:45 AM||||hi, my friend just bought a 87 GT through Ebay, 57k miles recent paint, great shape, 3500 bucks which I think is a great deal, the guy had it listed in the "collectibles" category which is why no one found out, sorry guys... but from now look there.<p>Anyways the car is in NJ, and we are in SF, CA so he will be driving it across, car is a 5sp and runs great, what should we check other than the basics to make sure it makes it ok, he wants to do 800 miles a day.<p>thanks
Z||000001||ChadMan||07-29-99||08:02 AM||||If it were me, I'd replace the ignition module in the distributor.  They seem to get cooked by the engine heat (my experience only - maybe that's just my Fiero!).  It's easy (30 min) and cheap ($30) and might save you from sitting dead along some interstate.<p>I recently delivered an 86 SE V6 from Columbus, OH to Phoenix - total repair bill was $8, picked up a nail in a tire.  Hope you have similar luck!
Z||000002||Phil||07-29-99||09:47 AM||||I wouldn't trust the gas gage.Fill it up right away and then at about 150 miles and see how much it takes, then make adjustments from there. I got stuck twice in a "new" 88GT  First time didn't know about the gage -empty at 1/4. Second time 150 miles on tripometer( the paint shop let it idle for who knows long to charge the battery)
Z||000003||lowCG||07-29-99||12:23 PM||||If the car has sat for any length of time,make sure the battery cables aren't corroded where they connect to the battery,ignition module is a good one,along with bringing some extra fuses,making sure that any wheel-lug locks are in the car,gas cap keys,air in the spare,jack,lug wrench.<br>If your friend want's to check out an S/E,V6,5spd,same year,with $1500 in recent reciepts for tune-up,module,brakes,shifter cables,there's a nice one in Maine for $1400.
Z||000004||ChadMan||07-29-99||01:52 PM||||Is it blue?  'Cause if it is, my wife just might have to accept a third Fiero out front.
Z||000005||theogre||07-29-99||02:36 PM||||Check the brakes, wheel bearings, and suspesion, thuroly. This isn't a trip to the groccer. Change the oil too.
Z||000006||lowCG||07-29-99||11:25 PM||||No,it's silver/grey,big factory wing thing,ocelot exhaust.
